      'Satellites: new “Tracking and rotator” page with sliders and boxes (default lead time 60 s instead of 150, tolerance, optional parking after the pass); with radios like the IC-820H no more flood of split and mode commands; there is an experimental two-VFO fallback (off by default) and you can choose the receive and transmit modes (not tested with real radio and rotator). Log: automatic ADIF saving with a switch (off by default) and a folder of your choice in Settings › Log, cluster and services › File; the aurora_log.adi file in the data folder is already written at every QSO. Before calling a station that is not among the recent decodes Aurora asks for confirmation (switch on by default). Radio: the SWR protection is in the Radio card, 2.0 by default (was 2.5), from 1.0 to 4.0 in steps of 0.1. Time: automatic clock correction is on by default (if you had turned it off you find it on once) and retries when the network returns; to change the Windows time Aurora must be started as administrator. WEFAX more compact (shorter selector, radio display and small waterfall on the same row, entry in the Mode menu of PSK·RTTY·CW). Help and What’s new are inside the Settings: the gear opens them directly on the PC (the phone does not change); the About page has the links in a grid and the clock warning can also be read by hovering over it.',
